Side CD of rectangle ABCD measures 12 meters, as shown. Each of the three triangles with a side along segment CD is an equilateral triangle. What is the total area of the shaded regions? Express your answer in simplest radical form. [asy]
import olympiad; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
fill((2,2*sqrt(3))--(4,0)--(6,2*sqrt(3))--cycle^^(6,2*sqrt(3))--(8,0)--(10,2*sqrt(3))--cycle,gray(0.7));
draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(12,2*sqrt(3))--(0,2*sqrt(3))--cycle);
draw((0,0)--(2,2*sqrt(3))--(4,0)--(6,2*sqrt(3))--(8,0)--(10,2*sqrt(3))--(12,0));
label("A",(0,2*sqrt(3)),NW); label("B",(12,2*sqrt(3)),NE); label("C",(12,0),SE); label("D",(0,0),SW);
draw("12 meters", (0,2*sqrt(3) + 1)--(12,2*sqrt(3) + 1),N);
[/asy]

Set R is a set of rectangles such that (1) only the grid points shown here are used as vertices, (2) all sides are vertical or horizontal and (3) no two rectangles in the set are congruent. If R contains the maximum possible number of rectangles given these conditions, what fraction of the rectangles in set R are squares? Express your answer as a common fraction. [asy]import graph;
size(50);
for(int i = 0; i<5; ++i)
for(int j = 0; j<5; ++j)
fill(Circle((i,j),.1));
[/asy]

The graph of y = f(x) is shown below.

[asy]
unitsize(0.3 cm);

real func(real x) {
 real y;
 if (x >= -3 && x <= 0) {y = -2 - x;}
 if (x >= 0 && x <= 2) {y = sqrt(4 - (x - 2)^2) - 2;}
 if (x >= 2 && x <= 3) {y = 2*(x - 2);}
 return(y);
}

int i, n;

for (i = -8; i <= 8; ++i) {
 draw((i,-8)--(i,8),gray(0.7));
 draw((-8,i)--(8,i),gray(0.7));
}

draw((-8,0)--(8,0),Arrows(6));
draw((0,-8)--(0,8),Arrows(6));

